# Patterns here are anchored to the context root unless they start with
# **/ — `dist/` matches ./dist and nothing under src/. The build-artifact,
# coverage and virtualenv lines below were written that way and so missed
# every one of the directories they were for: each service's dist/,
# node_modules/, coverage/ and *.tsbuildinfo, and the ai and engine-wrapper
# virtualenvs, all went to the daemon. The TypeScript images' build stages
# COPY whole service directories, so a host dist/ plus tsbuildinfo landed in
# the image, where `tsc -b` can judge the project up to date from them and
# skip the compile — shipping whatever the host last built. CI builds from a
# clean checkout, which is why it never showed there.

# Version control
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# CI/CD and infra (not needed in images)
.github/
infra/
e2e/

# Environment and secrets
.env*
!.env.example
keys/
*.pem
*.key

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Test and coverage artifacts
**/coverage/
**/.nyc_output/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.coverage
**/coverage.xml
mutants/
.mutmut-cache

# Build artifacts (rebuilt inside the image)
**/dist/
**/build/
**/node_modules/
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Python virtual environments (rebuilt inside the image)
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/

# Claude Code
.claude/

# Scratch / temp
**/scratchpad/
tmp/

# Local data and binary docs at the root
data/
*.docx

# Docker
Dockerfile*
docker-compose*.yml
.dockerignore

# Documentation
*.md
docs/
LICENSE
